// The development workspace: one checkout, three modules.
//
// `packages/` is the shared module both processes import, and each app has its
// own go.mod because each is its own binary with its own dependency graph — the
// gateway carries whatsmeow and no Temporal client, the backend the reverse.
//
// A workspace is a convenience for a checkout, not a build input: a Docker build
// does not read this file, which is why every go.mod also carries a `replace`
// pointing at the sibling copy of `packages/`. The two mechanisms say the same
// thing in the two places a build happens.
go 1.26.0

use (
	./apps/backend
	./apps/whatsapp-gw
	./packages
)
